<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dushanbe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Stalinabad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dushanbe is the capital and largest city of Tajikistan, on the Varzob river in the Hisor valley. A market village named after its Monday bazaar, it was chosen as capital of the Tajik ASSR in 1924 and grew rapidly as a planned Soviet city. It was called Stalinabad from 1929 to 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dushanbe.jpg" alt="Dushanbe" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adam Harangozó · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_with_buildings,_Dushanbe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
